  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 125 PM CDT Sat Sep 12 2026\n\nLittle change in the forecast with this update. Main concern \ncontinues to be heat across the region. With ridging building more \nover the area will maintain above normal temperatures with highs \nranging from the lower 90s along the coast to around 105-107 west. \nThe highest heat index values will be over the Coastal Plains and \ninto the Brush Country though, as dewpoints are highest over the \neast, with substantial mixing inland decreasing humidity. No real \nchange is expected in the MaxT forecast through at least the first \nhalf of the week. As moisture increases by mid-week, we could drop a \ndegree or two, but we'll remain above normal. \n\nIn terms of rainfall, for most of the area rain chances remain very \nlow (below 20%) for much of the period. The Victoria Crossroads does \nhave slightly higher chances at times (20-30%) where the higher \n(though still not much to get excited about) PWAT values reside. By \nWednesday or Thursday guidance still suggests a plume of moisture \nmoving into the region. The current PoPs may be a bit on the high \nend just based on recent patterns, but should see at least scattered \nshowers and storms for Thursday, especially east.",
